  "reviewed_source_delta": [
    "data_nodes only updates a comment. trip_planner_agent changes RAG graph ordering/candidate reuse, prompt time reservation and explicit disabled notice; no native loading, shell, endpoint or authority change.",
    "rag_service accepts already typed/validated POI candidates from internal state, deduplicates by POI id and writes bounded plain strings and source metadata through the same embedded store. No request-controlled collection config, remote embedding loader, new process, ctypes or native API dispatch.",
    "main only distinguishes configured-but-unavailable RAG from intentionally disabled. result_policy adds a nonretryable RAG_DISABLED reason. Authentication, upload boundary, fixed storage/index paths, embedded_settings and bounded Embeddings adapter are unchanged.",
    "All existing native file predicates match the candidate byte for byte; all bound dependency Python files unchanged. Application source hashes match actual image, including the five reviewed deltas. Existing absence/build/architecture/runtime constraints remain required by the gate; this record alone is not a gate pass."
  ],
  "new_findings": [
    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-100290",
      "packages": [
        "libc-bin",
        "libc6"
      ],
      "upstream_status": "unfixed",
      "classification": "not_affected_execution_path",
      "mechanism": "glibc POSIX regcomp/regexec realloc failure can leave dangling buffers and double-free under memory pressure.",
